# Memory Bank Protocol

Before non-trivial work, read `memory-bank/` in order:

1. `projectbrief.md`
2. `productContext.md`
3. `systemPatterns.md`
4. `techContext.md`
5. `activeContext.md`
6. `progress.md`

## Update policy (IWAS-style milestones)

- Update `activeContext.md` + `progress.md` at **task completion boundaries** (before the final milestone commit), not on every small edit.
- When the user says **update memory bank**, review ALL core files; focus on `activeContext.md` and `progress.md`.
- Keep Memory Bank token-lean. Archive old milestones under `memory-bank/archive/` instead of letting active files bloat.
- Permanent architecture invariants belong in durable docs (`strategies/README.md`, `reports/`, specs) — not only in Memory Bank scratch context.

## Language

- Memory Bank technical content: English preferred.
- User chat: Vietnamese OK.
